<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 20px; text-align: center;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Our Changing Forests – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;"><i>Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</i></p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 11th Grade (CEFR: B1.2)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Our Changing Forests</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> I Explored the Ecological History Of...</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Create informative articles on common interests. Interactive: Produce a collaborative story on local or global interest topics.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can create informative articles explaining local ecological changes and their impact on the community (e.g., "If the town plants more trees, the air quality will improve.")
            Can create informative articles about environmental conservation guidelines, listing actions to protect local forests (e.g., "If we prevent illegal logging, the forest ecosystem will recover faster.")
            Can work with peers to produce a story about ecological changes, incorporating community conservation efforts (e.g., "Over the past few years, our community has implemented several conservation projects that have significantly improved the local ecosystems.")</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> Students watch a 1-minute video clip or view a series of contrasting images showing a healthy forest versus a deforested area and then a reforested area. The teacher asks students to brainstorm words and phrases they remember from previous lessons related to these images. Teacher writes student suggestions on the board, activating vocabulary such as "deforestation," "biodiversity," "forest health," "conservation," "plant," "recover," "impact," "pollution." Students are prompted to consider the timeline of these changes.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models how to express ecological changes and conservation ideas in writing using target grammar. On the board, the teacher writes two example sentences:
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Deforestation <b>has significantly affected</b> biodiversity in our area over the past decade." (Highlighting Present Perfect, "significantly," "affected," "biodiversity").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"<b>If we prevent illegal logging</b>, the forest ecosystem <b>will recover faster</b>." (Highlighting First Conditional, "prevent," "illegal logging," "recover faster"). The teacher also practices the pronunciation of /aɪ/ in "life," "biodiversity" and "try", and the /ɪt/ sound in "climate."</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What verb tense did I use to talk about an action that started in the past and continues to affect the present?" (Expected answer: Present Perfect).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What does the second sentence suggest about what *will* happen if we stop illegal logging?" (Expected answer: The forest will get better, recover).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What's the meaning of 'biodiversity'?" (Expected answer: The variety of life in an ecosystem).</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Our Changing Forests".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Students read a short informative article (approx. 150-180 words) from a fictional environmental blog titled "Panama's Green Heart: A History of Change and Hope." The article discusses local ecological changes (e.g., deforestation near rivers, impact on marine life) and outlines community conservation efforts (e.g., planting native trees, promoting recycling). The text incorporates Present Perfect, First/Second Conditionals, and Comparatives, along with the target vocabulary.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Producing clear, detailed texts on a wide range of subjects related to their field of interest, summarizing information and arguments from various sources.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> Students answer the following questions after reading the article:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Question:</b> What is the main purpose of the article? (To inform about local ecological changes and conservation efforts).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Read the following statements and decide if they are True (T) or False (F) according to the article:
                        <ul style="list-style-type: circle; padding-left: 20px;">
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Urban ecosystems have increased biodiversity compared to natural habitats mentioned in the article."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"The community has implemented conservation projects that have improved local ecosystems."</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information Matching:</b> Match the ecological change with its corresponding conservation effort described in the article.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Writing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice writing sentences and short paragraphs using Present Perfect, First and Second Conditional, and Comparatives, incorporating vocabulary such as "deforestation," "biodiversity," "pollution," "rivers," "ecosystems," "conservation," "plant," "improve," "reduce," "affect," "recover," "healthier," "significant," "dramatic," "ecological," "illegal." Pragmatic function: discussing conservation ideas. Sociolinguistic function: expressing environmental concerns politely.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Sentence Completion (Controlled Practice):</b> Students complete sentences using the correct form of the verb in parentheses (Present Perfect) or choosing the appropriate conditional structure/comparative adjective.
                        <ul style="list-style-type: circle; padding-left: 20px;">
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Over the past few years, the community _____ (implement) several conservation projects."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If we _____ (reduce) plastic waste, marine life _____ (become) much healthier."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Rural areas usually have _____ (high) biodiversity _____ urban areas."</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Sentence Combination (Semi-controlled):</b> Students combine two given short sentences into one more complex sentence using First/Second Conditionals or Present Perfect, ensuring they use relevant vocabulary.
                        <ul style="list-style-type: circle; padding-left: 20px;">
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"People plant more trees. Forests recover faster." (Combine using Second Conditional: "If people planted more trees, forests would recover faster.")</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Illegal logging happened. It affected forest health." (Combine using Present Perfect: "Illegal logging has affected forest health.")</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Paragraph Expansion (Pair Interaction/Peer Check):</b> In pairs, students write 3-4 sentences describing a local ecological problem, using at least one Present Perfect and one conditional sentence, and 3-4 target vocabulary words. Then, they exchange their paragraph with another pair. The receiving pair highlights correctly used grammar and vocabulary and suggests one improvement for clarity or word choice. Emphasis on politely discussing conservation ideas (e.g., "Protecting our forests benefits everyone").</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-18 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Our Changing Forests".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative Informative Article Writing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students work in pairs or small groups (3 students) to create a short informative article (approx. 150-200 words) for a local environmental awareness campaign or school blog. The article should address the theme "I Explored the Ecological History Of..." focusing on "Our Changing Forests" in their imagined or real community.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Instructions:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Write an article that describes at least two significant ecological changes that have occurred in a local forest or natural area (using Present Perfect).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Propose at least two specific conservation guidelines or actions the community can take, explaining their potential impact (using First Conditional).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Include a comparison of the current state of the ecosystem to a healthier past or future (using Comparatives).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Integrate at least 8-10 target vocabulary words from the list (e.g., "deforestation," "biodiversity," "pollution," "conservation," "species," "ecosystems," "recover," "sustainable," "impact," "climate change").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">End with a community-focused call to action, politely expressing environmental concerns (e.g., "Together, we can make a difference in conservation.").</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The teacher circulates, providing support and monitoring accurate use of grammar and vocabulary. The focus is on clear communication of environmental issues and proposed solutions through writing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy and student self-assessment.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> The informative article created collaboratively in Stage 4.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Peer & Teacher Assessment):</b> Students will use a simplified rubric to assess their peers' articles, focusing on:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity and Cohesion:</b> Is the article easy to understand? Are ideas logically organized?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar Accuracy:</b> Accurate use of Present Perfect, First/Second Conditionals, and Comparatives.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary Use:</b> Appropriate and varied use of target environmental vocabulary.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Content Relevance:</b> Does the article address ecological changes and conservation efforts?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaborative Effort:</b> Evidence of teamwork in the writing process (if observed).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete two reflective prompts:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was the most challenging part of writing your article about ecological changes, and how did your group overcome it?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Which grammar structure (Present Perfect, conditionals, or comparatives) do you feel more confident using in your writing now?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection Prompts:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How effectively did we incorporate specific environmental concerns and community conservation efforts into our informative article today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one key message or piece of advice about protecting forests that you would want someone reading your article to take away?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What aspects of the collaborative writing task did students find most engaging? Was the length and complexity appropriate for a B1.2 level?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Were the scaffolding activities in Stage 3 sufficient for students to confidently produce their articles? What adjustments or additional support might be needed for students struggling with specific grammar points or vocabulary integration in writing?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Did students effectively use the target grammar (Present Perfect, conditionals, comparatives) and vocabulary in their written output? What common errors were observed that need further reinforcement?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson (Lesson 5: Mediation & Integration):</b> The informative articles created today will serve as foundational content. In the next lesson, students will mediate the information from these articles, possibly by summarizing them orally or in a different format, and integrating them into a larger 21st Century Skills Project focused on proposing solutions for local environmental challenges.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">2-3 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>